A||||6||BAM-BAM||Is this to much?||||5||
Z||000000||BAM-BAM||03-19-2000||12:24 AM||||  I was at the wrecking yard today and saw an<BR>87GT that had been hit hard in the nose. However, the engine is in emaculate condition. I asked "Bubba" what it would take for me to take the complete engine off his hands. He said $550.00 plus my core. Now, I have never purchased an engine before; is this to much? I figured you all might know better than I. BTW,  engine has 75,000 miles. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>  Thanx, BAM-BAM <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000001||Gokart||03-19-2000||05:31 AM||||What does he mean "with your core"! He wants it NOW if you decide to buy it tomorrow? My 2 cents says no good. I bought an entire parts car with a V6 for $250.00. If your looking for an engine to have rebuilt to have ready for when yours goes, find someone who doesn't want the core.||||reg||13
Z||000002||batboy||03-19-2000||06:15 AM||||That price is in the range of what they charge at the wreckers, maybe a little on the high end of the range. It depends a lot on the warranty, compression, and oil pressure (they did offer to show you those numbers, right?) Fiero heads are HO with bigger valves and are worth holding onto. I've never heard of a salvage yard wanting the core back, they must be selling them to a reman company and making a extra profit.<P>I'm like Gokart, I'd rather buy a whole car for that price. I see rusted out or wrecked Celebrities and Grand Ams (and sometimes ragged out Fieros too) for about $200 to $500 in running condition all the time. Grab the 2.8 out of it and any other parts you need, part out the rest of the car and crush whats left. Often you'll make most of your money back and have a nearly free engine.<p>[This message has been edited by batboy (edited 03-19-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||03-19-2000||09:47 AM||||I'm about to buy a 2.8 with 130,000 miles on it from a fellow forum member for $400 plus my motor.  Seems like a decent deal to me if it runs well.  (I know for sure that the motor I'm gonna buy runs well as it's the other members daily driver.)||||reg||1
Z||000004||88formula||03-19-2000||12:48 PM||||The going rate in New England for a ten year old engine with about 75000 miles is around five to six hundred dollars. I've never heard of them wanting a core in return though.||||reg||1
Z||000005||88formula||03-19-2000||12:56 PM||||If I were you and I was about to plant 6k on a used engine. I would find a good Camaro 3.4 60-degree v6 and plant that engine into my car instead. The 2.8’s are not worth the trouble. There is a 20% increase in displacement with the  3.4 engine over the 2.8 engine.||||reg||1
